  "codebook": {
    "definition": "Credit-claiming occurs when a senator explicitly attributes a positive outcome, action, or achievement to their own efforts, advocacy, or legislative work.",
    "clarification": "Credit-claiming is identified when a senator uses first-person language (e.g., 'I secured,' 'I announced,' 'I helped') or explicitly ties a positive result to their direct involvement. This includes securing funding, introducing or passing legislation, or advocating for a cause that leads to a tangible benefit for constituents or the nation. The focus is on the senator taking personal or direct responsibility for the outcome.",
    "positive_examples": [
      {
        "text": "Senator Dorgan announced Friday that U.S. Energy Secretary Samuel Bodman has officially designated Bismarck State College (BSC) as the National Power Plant Operations Technology and Educational Center. Dorgan said the designation is a recognition of the school's cutting-edge education and training program. This designation will help attract students, industry, and federal funding to help carry out BSC's mission. Dorgan authored legislation, which was signed into law, that created the National Center designation.",
        "explanation": "Senator Dorgan explicitly states that he authored the legislation that led to the designation of Bismarck State College as a National Center, directly claiming credit for this achievement."
      },
      {
        "text": "Sens. Barbara A. Mikulski and Benjamin L. Cardin (both D-Md.) today announced that the Allegany County Commissioners have been awarded a $294,980 Staffing for Adequate Fire and Emergency Response (SAFER) grant through the U.S. Department of Homeland Security's Assistance to Firefighters Grant Program (AFGP). Sen. Mikulski is on the Homeland Security Appropriations Subcommittee that funds the AFGP and fights each year to increase its federal funding.",
        "explanation": "Sens. Mikulski and Cardin explicitly announce the awarding of federal funding and tie it to Sen. Mikulski's role on the subcommittee that funds the program, directly claiming credit for their involvement in securing the grant."
      },
      {
        "text": "Sen. Jim Talent (R-Mo.) today announced that the Senate has approved his request for $1.5 million dollars for the Health Sciences Research and Education Facility at the University of Missouri-Columbia as part of the 2006 Energy and Water Appropriations bill.",
        "explanation": "Senator Talent explicitly states that the Senate approved his request for funding, directly claiming credit for securing the $1.5 million for the research facility."
      }
    ],
    "negative_clarification": "Credit-claiming does NOT occur when a senator discusses general positions, criticizes others, or provides information without explicitly tying a positive outcome to their own actions. Statements that are purely informative, critical, or commemorative do not qualify as credit-claiming unless they include a direct attribution of a positive result to the senator's efforts.",
    "negative_examples": [
      {
        "text": "The Bush Administration's 'head in the sand' position on global warming has defied reason and common sense. For six long years, it has suppressed scientists and scientific evidence, undermined international efforts to find solutions and delayed implementation of a strategy to protect the long-term interests of the nation.",
        "explanation": "The statement criticizes the Administration's position on global warming but does not claim credit for any specific action or achievement by the senator."
      },
      {
        "text": "Today we remember the brave Americans who lost their lives 65 years ago during the attacks on Pearl Harbor. Each year on December 7, we are reminded of the price our military men and women have paid to protect us and our freedoms.",
        "explanation": "The text commemorates Pearl Harbor and honors military service but does not claim credit for any specific action or achievement by the senator."
      },
      {
        "text": "The parliamentary elections in Iraq this week are an important step forward and I salute the bravery of the Iraqi people and our troops who are working to make these elections possible. However, a significant amount of work lies ahead after the elections if we are to make the crucial transition to place the future of Iraq squarely in the hands of the Iraqi people and allow our troops to come home.",
        "explanation": "The statement discusses challenges in Iraq but does not claim credit for any specific action or achievement by the senator."
      }
    ]
  }
}
